# Apixaban + 10 MeOH: cheap XTB2 pre-equilibration MD, WITH spherical confinement
# Analogous to Apixaban/Water/MD/Apixaban_10H2O_XTB_preequil_confined.inp
#
# Starting geometry: Apixaban_SMD_methanol_Opt_Freq_KeepDens.xyz (continuum
#   methanol-optimized Apixaban) + 10 MeOH monomers (from MeOH/Monomer.xyz),
#   each placed with its O atom on the same 12-direction, radius-12.78-Angstrom
#   sphere-shell pattern used for the original Explicit10H2O placement (offsets
#   reused verbatim, applied to this structure's own Apixaban centroid).
#   Orientation of each MeOH molecule is arbitrary (not hand-rotated) - the
#   confined MD is expected to relax any minor initial clashes and let the
#   molecules find real H-bonding/contact sites.
#   (Built programmatically; min initial solvent-Apixaban distance = 3.76
#   Angstrom, i.e. no clashes.)
#
# Cell Sphere: same confinement strategy as the water/DMSO runs - center =
#   Apixaban centroid of this structure (31.537, -19.865, -0.109; same as the
#   water/DMSO cases, since the solvent-optimized Apixaban geometries are nearly
#   identical), radius 14.0 Angstrom (Apixaban's own farthest atom from centroid
#   is ~9.0 Ang), spring constant 20 kJ/mol/Ang^2.
#
# Note: XTB2 is only used to generate a better-equilibrated starting geometry for
#   later r2SCAN-3c work - not for energetics used in the solvent comparison.

! XTB2 MD

%md
  Timestep 1.0_fs
  Initvel 298.15_K
  Thermostat NHC 298.15_K Timecon 20.0_fs
  Cell Sphere 31.537, -19.865, -0.109, 14.0 Spring 20
  Dump Position Stride 100 Filename "Apixaban_10MeOH_XTB_preequil_confined.xyz"
  Run 20000
end

